      "form_arabic": "فَيَرْكُمَهُ,",
      "lemma": "yarokuma",
      "lemma_arabic": "يَرْكُمَ",
      "pos": "V",
      "ayah_id": "8:37",
      "ayah_arabic": "لِيَمِيزَ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡخَبِيثَ مِنَ ٱلطَّيِّبِ وَيَجۡعَلَ ٱلۡخَبِيثَ بَعۡضَهُۥ عَلَىٰ بَعۡضࣲ فَيَرۡكُمَهُۥ جَمِيعࣰ ا فَيَجۡعَلَهُۥ فِي جَهَنَّمَۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Anfaal",
      "literal_gloss": "and heap them",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "[This is] so that Allah may distinguish the wicked from the good and place the wicked some of them upon others and heap them all together and put them into Hell. It is those who are the losers.",
        "pickthall": "That Allah may separate the wicked from the good, The wicked will He place piece upon piece, and heap them all together, and consign them unto hell. Such verily are the losers.",
        "khattab": "so Allah may separate the evil from the good. He will pile up the evil ones all together and then cast them into Hell. They are the ˹true˺ losers",
        "arberry": "that God may distinguish the corrupt from the good, and place the corrupt one upon another, and so heap them up all together, and put them in Gehenna; those are the losers."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        24,
        43,
        12
      ],
      "form_arabic": "رُكَامًا",
      "lemma": "rukaAm",
      "lemma_arabic": "رُكَام",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "24:43",
      "ayah_arabic": "أَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُزۡجِي سَحَابࣰ ا ثُمَّ يُؤَلِّفُ بَيۡنَهُۥ ثُمَّ يَجۡعَلُهُۥ رُكَامࣰ ا فَتَرَى ٱلۡوَدۡقَ يَخۡرُجُ مِنۡ خِلَٰلِهِۦ وَيُنَزِّلُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مِن جِبَالࣲ فِيهَا مِنۢ بَرَدࣲ فَيُصِيبُ بِهِۦ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَصۡرِفُهُۥ عَن مَّن يَشَآءُۖ يَكَادُ سَنَا بَرۡقِهِۦ يَذۡهَبُ بِٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرِ",
      "surah_revelation": "Medinan",
      "surah_name": "An-Noor",
      "literal_gloss": "(into) a mass",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Do you not see that Allah drives clouds? Then He brings them together, then He makes them into a mass, and you see the rain emerge from within it. And He sends down from the sky, mountains [of clouds] within which is hail, and He strikes with it whom He wills and averts it from whom He wills. The flash of its lightening almost takes away the eyesight.",
        "pickthall": "Hast thou not seen how Allah wafteth the clouds, then gathereth them, then maketh them layers, and thou seest the rain come forth from between them; He sendeth down from the heaven mountains wherein is hail, and smiteth therewith whom He will, and averteth it from whom He will. The flashing of His lightning all but snatcheth away the sight.",
        "khattab": "Do you not see that Allah gently drives the clouds, then joins them together, piling them up into masses, from which you see raindrops come forth? And He sends down from the sky mountains ˹of clouds˺ loaded with hail, pouring it on whoever He wills and averting it from whoever He wills. The flash of the clouds’ lightning nearly takes away eyesight",
        "arberry": "'hast thou not seen how God drives the clouds, then composes them, then converts them into a mass, then thou seest the rain issuing out of the midst of them? And He sends down out of heaven mountains, wherein is hail, so that He smites whom He will with it, and turns it aside from whom He will; wellnigh the gleam of His lightning snatches away the sight."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        52,
        44,
        9
      ],
      "form_arabic": "مَّرْكُومٌ",
      "lemma": "m~arokuwm",
      "lemma_arabic": "مَّرْكُوم",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "52:44",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَإِن يَرَوۡاْ كِسۡفࣰ ا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ سَاقِطࣰ ا يَقُولُواْ سَحَابࣱ مَّرۡكُومࣱ‏",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "At-Tur",
      "literal_gloss": "heaped up",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And if they were to see a fragment from the sky falling, they would say, \"[It is merely] clouds heaped up.\"",
        "pickthall": "And if they were to see a fragment of the heaven falling, they would say: A heap of clouds.",
        "khattab": "If they were to see a ˹deadly˺ piece of the sky fall down ˹upon them˺, still they would say, “˹This is just˺ a pile of clouds.”",
        "arberry": "Even if they saw lumps falling from heaven, they would say, 'A massed cloud!'"
      }
    }
  ]
